182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Nile International University runs remote exams for students in many governorates and countries. Commercial proctoring tools let the AI accuse students directly \(for example for looking away or background noise\), which students found unfair and biased. Some tools also collected far more personal data than needed, and there is no consistent, transparent process for accommodations, disconnections or appeals.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (It is recommended that a new proctoring system be developed in which the AI only flags events and humans make every decision affecting a student. It should be fair, transparent, privacy-respecting and connected to the learning management system \(LMS\), with a pilot during next semester's midterms.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 483 0 R
/E (Scheduling exams with a proctoring level \(1: screen, 2: plus webcam, 3: plus room scan and audio\), requiring at least Level 2 for exams over 30% of the grade, and applying accommodations automatically)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Showing students what data is collected and recording their consent before the exam)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 485 0 R
/E (Checking the system and student identity \(card vs. photo\), with manual video check by a live Proctor on failure, and booking campus testing-center seats)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 486 0 R
/E (Flagging events during the exam \(second face, leaving view, phone, other window, voices\) with a clip and severity score, never stopping the exam)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
